<title>MEXICO: Du Pont to invest $90 mln in Mexico plant.</title>
<headline>Du Pont to invest $90 mln in Mexico plant.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>E.I. Du Pont de Nemours' Mexican subsidiary will invest $90 million in a new solid waste treatment plant on the Gulf of Mexico, an industry spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>&quot;The investment is earmarked for a second extension to the company's facilities in the Tampico-Altamira industrial corridor,&quot; said Dora Trevino Cantu, head of promotion at the Business Center in Gulf of Mexico port Tampico.</p>
<p>Trevino said the plant would reprocess waste into iron oxides for use in the paint industry.</p>
<p>-- Debora Montesinos, Monterrey newsroom +528 345-7677</p>
